## INFERENCE POLICY (Mode A — v1.2 LLM-Native)

The lean flow's central principle: **LLM infers first, asks second, never re-asks**.

### Mode Detection (Phase 0)
```
IF user provides .eml file OR pastes email text OR describes a screenshot
  → Mode A (Reference)
ELSE
  → Mode B (Fresh)
```
Auto-detected at the start of Phase 0 — the agent does not ask "are you in Mode A?".

### LLM-Extracted (Mode A only — no script invocation)
The LLM reads the reference content directly and extracts:
- Subject components (prefix, date, project name, status color, region)
- Sender name (from "Thanks\\n{name}" sign-off)
- CC list (from .eml headers when available)
- Status colors (Overall Delivery + GDC Project)
- Section content (Summary, Completed, In Progress, Ask, Attention)
- Metric values (Capacity %, User Story %, per-phase Days/Defects/DpD)
- Team labels (Team 1, Team 2, ...)
- Workstream names (Build / Design / UAT Support / Business Go live)

> **Why no script (v1.2 change)?** Modern LLMs read structured/semi-structured email text far more flexibly than regex. The dropped `prior_email_parser.py` only handled the specific Heineken-like format; the LLM handles arbitrary formats.

### Always Auto-Set (both modes)
- **Date** — always today via `date "+%d-%b-%y"` — NEVER asked
- **Time-stamped output folder** — `{YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm}_{project-slug}/`
- **Active team roster** — from `team-roster.yaml`

### Asked in the Phase 1 Single Batch (always)
- Leaves/holidays this week (`Name=days_off, ...` or `none`)
- Jira paste or metric description (LLM parses natively)
- Free-form section updates / additions / removals
- (Conditional) sycophancy nudge if status–blockers contradict in either direction

