## TEMPLATE-DRIVEN RULES

### Core Sections (all phases)
Generate ONLY sections where `body_sections[].required: true` — all WSR body sections ARE required; none may be omitted.

### Missing Data Handling
- NEVER default values or invent content
- If a required field is empty → render section header with `⚠️ MISSING — please provide {field}` inline
- LLM aggregates all `⚠️ MISSING` markers into the inline chat list at SP2 AND into `run_metadata.json`'s `gaps[]` array

### Metric Naming (ZERO tolerance — script-enforced)
- `Capacity Utilisation` — British `s`, always `%` (`british_spelling_linter`)
- `User Story Delivered` — exact phrase, always `%` (`metric_name_validator`)
- `Defects Per Days` — decimal, NEVER `%` (`numeric_format_validator`)

### Subject Line (constructed in Phase 2)
Must match `subject_regex`; validated by `subject_line_validator.py` (covers completeness in v1.2).

### Recipient Line (rendered at handoff — LLM checks)
```
TO: gdc-project-collaboration@salesforce.com
CC: {user_provided_cc OR inherited from reference}
⚠️ REMINDER: Open email_body.html in browser, copy-paste into Gmail. Compose a FRESH email. Do NOT Reply or Forward.
```

